  "result": "Perfect! All 179 tests pass. I've successfully added payment terms support to the invoicing system:\n\n## What was added:\n\n**src/errors.js** \u2014 Added `TERMS_INVALID` error:\n- Returns when terms are not one of: NET14, NET30, EOM\n\n**src/dates.js** \u2014 Added `lastDayOfMonth(dateStr)` function:\n- Calculates the last day of the month for end-of-month payment terms\n\n**src/invoices.js** \u2014 Enhanced `createInvoice`:\n- Accepts optional `terms` parameter (defaults to 'NET30')\n- Returns `invoice.terms` and `invoice.dueDate` \n- Supports three term types:\n  - **NET14**: due 14 days after issue date\n  - **NET30**: due 30 days after issue date (default)\n  - **EOM**: due on last day of the issue month\n- Validates terms and returns `TERMS_INVALID` for unknown values\n\n**test/invoices.test.js** \u2014 Added 13 tests:\n- Default NET30 and explicit term selection\n- NET14, NET30, EOM calculations\n- Month and year boundary handling\n- Invalid term rejection\n\n**test/dates.test.js** \u2014 Added 8 tests:\n- Last day calculations for each month type\n- Leap year handling\n- Edge cases (first/last day of month)\n\nAll 179 tests pass with no regressions.",
